<title>SOUTH AFRICA: REX TRUEFORM YR SHARE LOWER, DIV STATIC.</title>
<headline>REX TRUEFORM YR SHARE LOWER, DIV STATIC.</headline>
<dateline>CAPE TOWN 1996-09-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Yr to June 30, 1996</p>
<p>		    (millions of rands unless stated)</p>
<p>    Shr (cts)	     57.8     vs  60.3</p>
<p>    Yr div (cts)	  20	 vs  20</p>
<p>    Attrib income	 10.25    vs  10.23</p>
<p>    Before tax	    16.47    vs  14.03</p>
<p>    Tax			6.22    vs   3.79</p>
<p>    Interest received    2.44    vs   1.56</p>
<p>    Turnover	     212.57    vs 192.35</p>
<p>Div payable: To be advised</p>
<p>On register: Nov 8</p>
<p>Name - Rex Trueform Clothing Company Ltd </p>
<p>NOTE - The clothing and textile company said shareholders would be given the option of receiving &quot;N&quot; ordinary shares in lieu of the cash dividend.</p>
<p>The group said its financial position was strong and it was well placed to benefit from the further planned expansion of its Queenspark division in the coming year.</p>
<p>-- Cape Town +27 21 25-2238</p>
</text>
